      "raw": "<p>We&#39;ve had the situation come up where Iron Legacy plays a one shot which has wording roughly &quot;Each player must either discard 2 cards or destroy one of their cards in play&quot;</p><p>My understanding is that the hero cards themselves aren&#39;t cards in playt. I don&#39;t have an absolute certainty of this, but I recall another card that basically says &quot;destroy all your cards in play or dicard your hand&quot; so I assumed your hero wasn&#39;t included as the choice would be between &quot;kill your hero or discard your hand&quot;.&nbsp;</p><p>In the game, we decided to &quot;choose&quot; to destroy something, then found nothing to destroy. That may not have been allowed, but we had also been hit by multiple bad memories or whatever the &quot;everyone discard, play another villain card&quot; one is called. I don&#39;t even think we could discard two at that point.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>So I guess my questions are:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Can you choose an option you can&#39;t really fulfill? Would he blow up your character if it&#39;s the only card out?&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
